  "limitations": [
    "Human-05 fitted the persona; all reported comparisons to it are in-sample. Different agent seeds do not create held-out human participants.",
    "These three new native review attempts do not include earlier historical development failures and do not establish a population success rate.",
    "Native CPU is a sampled diagnostic estimate with uncontrolled background work and app sessions, not a controlled statistical or energy result. Runs 01/02 precede the collector metadata-cache change; run 03 includes it.",
    "Core benchmark batches use the generic legacy persona in simulation, with real-time sleeps and the OS sampler excluded; they are not native throughput. Some intermediate batches overlapped native work. Final core/holdout batches followed GUI completion.",
    "Metadata caching retains 0.5-second configured PID/CPU/RSS/thread sampling. A known nonmatching PID that execs or is reused without being absent between samples can take up to the 5-second metadata refresh to be reclassified; matched PID reuse is checked per sample.",
    "Serial keyboard delivery cannot reproduce overlapping key holds; pauses, pointer sampling and process-pattern similarity remain limited."
  ],
